R1  per-generator integrated QNEC -> the tree's [S'] formula
  INT_A^B S'' dlambda == S'(B) - S'(A)   (FTC, sympy)                      ok
  Q_-(A,B) >= 0 is INT_A^B T >= (1/2pi)[S'(B)-S'(A)]  (same expression)    ok

R2  z3: the boundary hypothesis is load-bearing
  QNEC + S'(start)=S'(end)=0 + sum T < 0 : UNSAT                           ok
  QNEC + [S'] >= 0 + sum T < 0 : UNSAT  ([S'] >= 0 already suffices)       ok
  QNEC + [S'] = -1 + sum T < 0 : SAT  (ANEC can fail)                      ok
      witness: sum T = -0.0796, [S'] = -1  (sum T >= [S']/2pi = -0.1592)
