R3  null-plane modular identity: what QNEC adds to ANEC
  dK'(b) = -2pi INT_b^inf T                                                ok
  dK''(b) = 2pi T(b)                                                       ok
  (a) S_rel'' = 2pi (T - dS''/2pi): QNEC <=> convexity of S_rel            ok
  (b) 2pi ANE = [S_rel'] + [dS']                                           ok
  (c) with [dS']=0, S_rel'(+inf)=0: ANE = -S_rel'(-inf)/2pi >= 0 by monotonicity ok
  explicit T(x): negative somewhere (T(0) = -1/2) yet ANE = 0.58346 > 0    ok
  QNEC-saturating dS has [dS'] = 2pi ANE (!= 0): boundary term need not vanish ok
      i.e. integrated QNEC then reads ANE >= ANE: consistent but vacuous; the
      conclusion INT T >= 0 comes from [S'] = 0, a hypothesis on the state.

